I ran out of food, so, since my current game plan
didn't include a pet, or moving more than a step or
two across well trodden territory, I deliberately
ate a violet fungus. Ah, the joys of hallucination.
I was altar-sticking, so when I took a swing at what
looked like a garter snake on the altar of Kos, what
to my wondering eyes should appear:

The munchies are interfering with your motor capabilities.
The sour blade draws life from the microscopic space fleet.
You kill the gray unicorn.
You are splashed by the battlemech's acid!
Your Stormbringer is not affected.

This rogue has never been off dungeon level one.
Here is what the _opposite_ of the protection
racket looks like:

Desiring the Rogue  St: 10 Dx:18 Co: 18 In: 12 Wi:14 Ch:9 Chaotic
Dlvl:1 $:0 HP:59(65) Pw:50(50) AC:1 XP:9/2631 T:39706 Weak Hallu

I figure going to level 2 before I extinguish
everything nasty is suicide, so I, Stormbringer,
Sting, 22 +0 daggers, and this altar are married for
a few hundred thousand turns. There's some trivial
amount of gold in a sack behind me, mostly death
dropped by dwarves in single digit quantities and
both entrances to this room are in a direct line of
dagger flight. I'm wearing entirely death dropped
armor, all from Dwarfs except for a +1 iron skull
cap from an Uruk-Hai. Life is good, but dying with
this XL is just too easy. Luckily, Stormbringer is
being nice about offing giant ants quickly.  I only
know a couple of scrolls, by risky random testing;
luckily, the second one was identify.

I was of two minds about Sting, since I had a runed
dagger already, but I let it be Kos' second gift
instead, in hopes it would be rustproof on arrival;
Stormbringer, received before the ID scroll, was.

Patience: what I came to this game to learn.

I'm figuring my YAAD will  be due to not having
reflection, and some nasty showing up with a wand
of instadeath, but it will be a good run while it
lasts.

